pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% The structure control for the deletion route: the identical proof with the `proofgoal 1`
% wrapper deleted. The deletion obligation is then really checked and the proof is refused --
% by the UNFIXED checker too. So what forged the verdict is the fabricated goal, not "checked
% deletion is broken".
f 2 ;
strengthening_to_core on;
delc 2 : : subproof
qed;
sol x1 ;
output NONE;
conclusion SAT ;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
